WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.801
-Thank you, thank you so much
for coming on.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:03.968
It's always great to see you.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.367
And I just want
to really thank you,

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.267
because this must be hard

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.667
for you guys because you lost
one of your founding

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:16.868
members of De La Soul, Dave, not
less than a month ago.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.901
I know this
is a tough time for you,

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.067
but you making the trip
to come on our show

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:23.634
and talk to everybody,
and talk about Dave

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.968
and talk about De La Soul
means a lot to us,

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.267
but also to the fans out there.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.801
This means a lot.
Thank you.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.400
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.067
Yeah, man.
It's bittersweet, you know?

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.901
-It's got to be bittersweet
because you've been trying

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.000
to get your stuff
available for years.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.067
-Yeah.
-About a good 15 years.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.767
-I remember having -- we had you
on in "Late Night."

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.834
We talked about that with Dave,

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.601
and we had you on
"Tonight Show" as well.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.868
I go, "Is it out yet?"
"Jimmy, hold on.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:52.901
Wait a sec."
We're almost there.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.234
It's coming."
-Almost, yeah.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:57.167
-"Almost." finally, it's
available on Spotify, anything.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.834
You get De La Soul, type it in,
stream it.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.934
Give it to everybody.
It's finally...

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.534
Yo.
-Yeah, Dave.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:07.567
-Dave, they're doing it.
-Yeah, man.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.033
-What do you --
what do you remember

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:12.534
about this debut, the first one?

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:14.234
-I remember me having hair.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:17.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.234
-Cutting high school
my last year.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.434
-Is that right?

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.767
-To make that record.
-To make this record.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.501
-I was supposed
to graduate in '88.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.767
I ended up graduating in '89
because I cut.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.033
-Because of this.
-To make that record.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.801
-Did you guys --
did you meet in school?

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:31.968
-Yeah.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.000
-Summer school.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:35.868
-Is that right?

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.000
-I was trying
to get extra credit.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.601
-Yeah.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.801
-No, he wasn't.
-No, he wasn't. Yeah.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.701
-We were all failing English.
-Yeah.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.200
-We had to take
an English class.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.100
-That's interesting.
That's where you guys met.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.100
-Yeah, yeah, I mean, I've known
Dave through his brother, Mike.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.033
So, by me moving from the Bronx
to Long Island,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:55.501
met Mike Jolicoeur,
and that's how I met Dave.

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.601
Yeah, we just became cool,
and of course,

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.167
hip hop just embraced us.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.767
-What school in Long Island?

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.534
-Amityville.
-Amityville High School.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.501
Amityville Junior High
and High School.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.200
-Amityville.
Amityville's in the house.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.367
-Amityville.
-Yeah, we got some Long Island.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.200
So many people have said this
album changed their life,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.901
including Questlove,
who it changed him.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:19.834
Quest, how -- how did it
change your life?

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.467
-I mean, for the first time,
we just saw, like, ourselves.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:25.367
This is how, like,
the group bonded, Tariq and I.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.901
We just saw three friends just
having fun with each other,

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.234
practical jokes
and all that stuff.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.767
And we had never seen that in
hip hop before.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:33.801
-Yeah.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.267
-Do you guys feel
like you were being free

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:38.234
when you were making this
and rhyming.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:41.601
-Definitely, cause we were just
having fun in Mase's basement,

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:44.067
and it literally went from the
basement to the studio

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.234
because by the luck of the draw

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:47.734
we have someone
like Prince Paul.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.834
-Yeah, Prince Paul.
-Implemented that freedom.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:50.934
-Yeah.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:51.934
-How did you hook up
with Prince Paul?

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.234
Just through a label?

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.968
-No, he was from Amityville.
-He's from Amityville.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.601
He went from -- yeah.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:03:00.968
-Yeah, I used to do a bunch of
parties around Long Island,

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.634
and Paul come
from the battle scene.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.701
So, he would come to these
parties and deejay for about

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.968
20 minutes,
and do all his tricks

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.667
until somebody went
to pop a tape in.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.133
And he would stop, take the
tape, pop it out and leave.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.467
That's how -- that's how, yeah.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:16.968
-He say don't play my tape.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.100
-You know, he didn't want nobody
biting his tricks.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.100
He didn't want nobody
stealing his tricks.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.601
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.534
And Paul was part of the
legendary group Stetsasonic.

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:26.834
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.334
-And how crazy enough
that they're from Brooklyn,

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.901
he's from Long Island.
-Yeah, I didn't know that.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.334
-Yeah, I moved from Brooklyn
to Long Island,

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.901
and here it is,
I moved closer to my dream

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:37.434
by meeting Prince Paul.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:40.033
-What was the basement like?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.934
Do you remember the basement?
-The basement?

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.334
-Yeah, your basement.
-My basement?

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:44.801
Oh, it was very dark.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.067
-Did you have anything
to sit on? What was it?

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:52.567
-We had stuff to sit on because
my uncle made it, like,

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:56.000
a little sanctuary where he
would bring his girlfriends.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.200
and all that.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.901
-Wow.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.467
-It was beautiful.
-But then I took over

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.267
with the records
and the equipment.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.367
-And you started taking over.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.267
I have a picture of you guys
back then.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:13.000
Look at this.
-Oh.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.300
-Yeah.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.934
I refuse to wear those pants.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.801
-Yeah, why didn't you -- why
didn't you wear the pants?

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:21.067
-I wasn't with it, man.
-That was dope though.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.968
-That was our first performance.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:25.234
Yeah, man.
We were scared.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.834
DMC was right up front,
cheering us on.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.734
-DMC was there.
Jay was there.

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:30.734
-Yeah.
-What?

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.434
-Kane was there.
-No.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:34.167
I wouldn't have --
I wouldn't have gone on.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.601
"You've got to get out of here,
and then let us perform."

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:41.267
And what were they like after
you guys performed?

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.567
-They loved it, man.
It was actually Stesasonic's

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.567
release party, but we got to
perform at it.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.901
And we did the one song, and I
remember DMC came backstage,

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.501
was like,
"Yo, do the song again."

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:51.801
Like, it was just amazing.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:54.033
-And it was -- yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.501
It was at Urban Plaza, yep.

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:58.267
-Was that Urban Plaza?
-Urban plaza, yep.

00:04:58.267 --> 00:05:00.234
-Urban Plaza here in the city.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:04.567
I know it's been years and years
just legal battles

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.067
trying to get this thing out.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.567
I just want to let
everyone know a couple

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.033
accolades about this album.

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.267
University recognizing one of
the best and most influential

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.734
albums in hip hop history.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.667
One of the greatest
albums of all time.

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.200
"Rolling Stone" listed as one
of the 200 greatest

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.434
hip hop albums of all time
at number 33.

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:21.501
Library of Congress added
the album to the National

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:24.601
Recording Registry for its
for cultural significance.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.634
Since it was released,
it is now -- right now currently

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:30.467
number 15 on the Billboard
200 album chart.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:31.667
It is back.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.934
De La Soul is back!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.634
I love you guys, and thank you
for playing.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:36.634
You're going to play
with The Roots tonight?

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:39.901
-Yes, of course.
-"Stakes Is High."

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.767
-I would like to thank --
I would like to thank

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:45.234
Reservoir Media for making this
all possible.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.234
-Okay.
-The new owners,

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.534
people who actually bought
the catalog who made

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:52.133
the deal extremely right
for us, you know?

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.133
-That's awesome.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:54.767
-And I also want to thank --

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:57.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.501
I also want to thank Dave.

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.133
-Want to thank Dave.
-I want to thank Dave.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.634
I want everybody -- can you
please say for me,

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:05.701
"Thank you, Dave?"

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.501
-Thank you, Dave!

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.300
-Thank you.
-Come on.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.133
Tonight he's watching.
-Yeah, man.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.701
-Check out De La Soul's entire
back catalog available now

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:14.701
on all streaming platforms.

